05d7f82c89ad42bbb983ac36e265ad13,efd1d3ef3fbf45ff9e3a4478ed8cf5bd,lin2014microsoft8,c_92claw,ai,True,False,True,lin2014microsoft,Supported,medium,other,False,False,3,"In our experiments with COCO we predict 3 boxes at each scale so the tensor is $N N $ for the 4 bounding box offsets, 1 objectness prediction, and 80 class predictions.",True,,"We present a new dataset with the goal of advancing the state-of-the-art in object recognition by placing the question of object recognition in the context of the broader question of scene understanding. ||| The Microsoft Common Objects in COntext (MS COCO) dataset contains 91 common object categories with 82 of them having more than 5,000 labeled instances, Fig. 6. ||| We introduce a new large-scale dataset that addresses three core research problems in scene understanding: detecting non-iconic views (or non-canonical perspectives [12]) of objects, contextual reasoning between objects and the precise 2D localization of objects."
05d7f82c89ad42bbb983ac36e265ad13,efd1d3ef3fbf45ff9e3a4478ed8cf5bd,lin2017feature7,c_1j5zzbe,ai,True,False,True,lin2017feature,Supported,medium,other,False,False,2,Our system extracts features from those scales using a similar concept to feature pyramid networks.,True,,"Feature pyramids are a basic component in recognition systems for detecting objects at different scales. ||| We evaluate our method, called a Feature Pyramid Network (FPN), in various systems for detection and segmentation [11, 29, 27]."
