668e0024b0814d9181768736da410902,8991236a1afc41928d5e2e144f0e2a43,graves2006ctc10,c_lcwlr1,ai,True,False,True,graves2006ctc,Supported,high,background,False,False,4,"CTC~ defines a sequence-level objective that marginalizes over all monotonic alignments between input acoustic frames and output label sequences, producing frame-level posterior probabilities over output tokens and a blank symbol.",True,,"From Network Outputs to Labellings A CTC network has a softmax output layer (Bridle, 1990) with one more unit than there are labels in L. ||| The total probability of any one label sequence can then be found by summing the probabilities of its different alignments. ||| Finally, we use B to define the conditional probability of a given labelling l ∈L≤T as the sum of the probabilities of all the paths corresponding to it: p(l|x) = X π∈B−1(l) p(π|x). (3) 3.2. ||| The activations of the first |L| units are interpreted as the probabilities of observing the corresponding labels at particular times."
668e0024b0814d9181768736da410902,8991236a1afc41928d5e2e144f0e2a43,kuchaiev2019nemo9,c_1ylbfc8,ai,True,False,True,kuchaiev2019nemo,Supported,high,other,False,False,2,Forced alignment is performed using Connectionist Temporal Classification (CTC) models implemented in NVIDIA NeMo~.,True,,"NeMo is built around neural modules, conceptual blocks of neural networks that take typed inputs and produce typed outputs. ||| NeMo: a toolkit for building AI applications using Neural Modules Oleksii Kuchaiev, Jason Li, Huyen Nguyen, Oleksii Hrinchuk, Ryan Leary, Boris Ginsburg, Samuel Kriman, Stanislav Beliaev, Vitaly Lavrukhin, Jack Cook, Patrice Castonguay, Mariya Popova, Jocelyn Huang, Jonathan M."
668e0024b0814d9181768736da410902,8991236a1afc41928d5e2e144f0e2a43,radford2022whisper1,c_x42mgo,ai,True,False,True,radford2022whisper,Supported,high,background,False,False,2,"Although self-supervised and weakly supervised pretraining has improved general ASR performance (e.g., wav2vec~2.0~ and Whisper~), domain mismatch remains a major source of error, motivating the need for recent, domain-specific speech resources.",True,,"In this work we close that gap, scaling weakly supervised speech recognition the next order of magnitude to 680,000 hours of labeled audio data. ||| We demonstrate models trained at this scale transfer well to existing datasets zeroshot, removing the need for any dataset-specific fine-tuning to achieve high-quality results."
