a4bcdb84de344556b9b29545fb3b4608,6bcc9f6f32df4b59a427e4cd83381f61,radford2019language15,c_2g2wyv,ai,True,False,True,radford2019language,Partially Supported,low,background,False,False,1,"For the 3975 useful NQ development set questions, we found that the poor results of using GPT-2-117M unaided reported in were born out.",True,,"GPT-2 answers 4.1% of questions correctly when evaluated by the exact match metric commonly used on reading comprehension datasets like SQUAD.3 As a comparison point, the smallest model does not exceed the 1.0% accuracy of an incredibly simple baseline which returns the most common answer for each question type (who, what, where, etc...)."
a4bcdb84de344556b9b29545fb3b4608,6bcc9f6f32df4b59a427e4cd83381f61,radford2019language2,c_gjgifj,ai,True,False,True,radford2019language,Supported,medium,background,False,False,2,"At the other extreme, the ability of the GPT-2 model to answer factoid questions, based purely on unsupervised training directed at improving its Language Model (LM) performance, was striking.",False,The cited paper introduces and talks about GPT-2.,"Our largest model, GPT-2, is a 1.5B parameter Transformer that achieves state of the art results on 7 out of 8 tested language modeling datasets in a zero-shot setting but still underfits WebText. ||| We demonstrate that language models begin to learn these tasks without any explicit supervision when trained on a new dataset of millions of webpages called WebText."
